  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable aquaculture in the northern region of Angola (PPG)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will follow an Ecosystem Approach to Aquaculture (EAA) in the northern provinces of Uige, Bie, Bengo, Cuanza Norte and Malanje (tentative), which together cover a total area of 266,310km2 and represent 64% of Angolas family aquaculture units .

The project aligns with the Food System Integrated Program&apos;s (FS IP) overarching objective by adopting an innovative, socially inclusive, integrated and sustainable approach to food systems that secures global environmental benefits, while improving livelihoods, employment, entrepreneurship and food security, and supporting accelerated socio-economic growth in Angola. It will deliver this through four components that will help ensure that the proposed expansion of the aquaculture sub-sector in Angola is environmentally, socially and economically sustainable.</narrative>
  </description>
